+ * A VMD whose registers read as nothing did not come back, and fails at
+ * once.  The configuration register is written back first, since it
+ * decides the buses the VMD's configuration space reaches.  Every port is
+ * resumed even after one failed; a failure is reported as EIO, never as
+ * ESTALE, since a VMD cannot be attached afresh.
